WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
The healthiest diet is
one that maximizes

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.800
the intake of
foods-as-grown—

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.120
whole, plant-based foods—

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.860
and minimizes the
intake of processed

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.540
and animal-
based foods.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.580
In the first half of my
book, How Not to Die,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.920
I cover the “why” of
eating healthfully,

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.260
exploring the role diet may
play in the prevention,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.060
treatment, and sometimes
even reversal

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.340
of the fifteen leading
causes of death

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.360
in the United States.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.480
In the second half,
I dive into the “how”

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.680
of eating healthfully,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.380
which includes my
Daily Dozen checklist.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.660
The Daily Dozen
was developed

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.580
based upon the best available
balance of evidence.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.880
Rather than being a meal
plan or diet in itself,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.400
it’s really just a
checklist to inspire you

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.620
to include some of the
healthiest of healthy foods

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.660
into your daily routine.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.820
It may appear to
be a lot of boxes,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.100
but it’s easy to check
off a bunch at a time.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.083
For example, my
“groatnola” recipe,

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:50.880
which you can find

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.980
on the NutritionFacts.org
recipe page,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.160
nails whole grains, berries,
and nuts &amp; seeds,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.074
in one shot.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.720
The checklist can help
you think about

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.880
how you can improve
the nutrient density

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.920
of your meals and it can
also help you design

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.540
a more balanced meal.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.583
Note, the Daily Dozen is
just meant to serve

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:11.220
as an aspirational
minimum.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.540
Feel free to add
even more

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.024
Green Light foods
throughout your day.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.460
We created the Daily
Dozen Challenge

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.620
to help more people
discover how to include

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.600
some of the best foods
into their daily life.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.660
Pick a day to eat
the Daily Dozen,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.280
and document it
on social media.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.020
Share your challenge
experience

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.060
with friends and family
to help inspire more people

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.860
to include some of
the healthiest whole,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.360
plant foods into
your meals.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.120
Use the hashtag
#DailyDozenChallenge

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.340
on all your posts to
help build a community

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.780
of people taking
the challenge

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.060
and inspire even
more people to join.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.100
Together, we can help
encourage more people

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.613
to adopt healthier habits.

